{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789329320,"nonce":"/iEJmw03mqkB6EnrXMBbyyqJvIo=","title":"Trivial setters are never recognised","message":"mir_trivial_setter_field accepted only a body whose return value is the\nset_field instruction's own result. The builder lowers `v=(x) { _v = x }`\nas `v2 = move v1; v3 = set_field v0, #0, v2; return v2`: the return is\nthe argument's alias, so every setter came back None. The interpreter's\ntrivial-setter dispatch, the ObjFn setter field and the promotion\npass's setter recognition were all dead for real code.\n\nFix: accept a return of the argument or its alias as well.","files":null}]}